The first thing cha affects is whether you can decide about the removal of
your armor. When you prepare a safe room for dancing in, which you should do
anyway, that isn't a problem. Your body armor you _want_ removed anyway, the
rest you just put on again after the encounter.
The probability of a positive effect is (Int+Cha+1)/35, so with an int of,
say, 18 and a cha of 8 (randomly picked as "typical", somewhat low  wizard 
starting values) you already have a 77% chance of a good outcome. Since you
can have quite some encounters before the foocubus cancels, you can somewhat
rely on the law of large numbers. With that and a unicorn horn, there's not
much to fear, really.

